    "narrative": "The top of our rotation for LawDog today is anchored by **Lawrence Butler** (71.26) and **Bryson Stott** (71.23), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups against back-end starters. **Lawrence Butler** projects as our elite offensive engine, capitalizing on a 3.98 xERA matchup against P\u00e9rez and a clean middle-of-the-order spot. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** remains a must-start; while we typically penalize him for an \"Elite Hold SP\" risk\u2014where an opposing pitcher\u2019s skill set might stifle our stolen base potential\u2014the projection reflects a significant platoon advantage against Avila that makes his 71.23 score too high to fade. **Taylor Ward** also deserves recognition as a tier-one play (71.19), as he avoids the \"lefty-lefty\" disadvantage against Lodolo to provide significant power upside.\n\nThe lineup construction strategy prioritizes the scarcity of stolen bases. We have strategically positioned **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.69) and **Drew Gilbert** (50.86) to exploit Gordon\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a tangible boost to our stolen base probability. While **Daulton Varsho** (52.12) is currently operating near our marginal floor, his inclusion remains necessary to hedge against the volatility of the bottom-third of the order. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets**, who posted a respectable 48.63 score against Sheehan. Ultimately, the optimizer favored **Geraldo Perdomo** (59.18) due to his superior position in the batting order and his higher baseline efficiency, keeping **Gavin Sheets** on the pine to preserve our game caps.\n\nWe are monitoring several situational risks as the day progresses. The primary concern remains the health of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains on the IL, leaving a significant void in our power production. Additionally, we are tracking the weather closely for any games that might suppress output, though the current projections do not indicate any major disruptions. We are proceeding with **Cal Raleigh** (63.15) and **Jonathan Aranda** (67.67) as reliable staples; however, we will be watching their early at-bats closely against Yesavage and Lambert to ensure their dynamic platoon adjustments align with the game-flow. Other rostered assets like **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Will Smith**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Tyler Freeman** are currently held in reserve, ready to be deployed as matchups shift throughout the week.",
